A more careful version would show a value only for purchases, as in `=IF(E2<0,ABS(E2),"")`. That mirrors F's pattern, but the header says "Absolute Value of Purchase", and the simplest reading is `=ABS(E2)`. Since F already blanks out the non-payments, the matching approach for G is to show the absolute value only when E is negative.

{"formula": "=IF(E2<0,ABS(E2),\"\")"}

